WEBVTT

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.000
<i>The world was burning.</i>

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.080
<i>Like it was being cremated.</i>

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:49.040
<i>On the brink of death...</i>

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.450
<i>I saw God.</i>

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.200
<i>When finishing them,</i>
<i>always aim for the neck.</i>

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:08.410
<i>Because that is the only part</i>
<i>that remains human till the end.</i>

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:12.120
<i>Exterminators must wield</i>
<i>a heartless sword.</i>

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:14.950
<i>If you swing your sword for anger</i>
<i>or passion,</i>

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:16.700
<i>your blade will shatter,</i>

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.910
<i>and it will soon slice your own throat.</i>

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.000
I know.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:26.040
That's why I took his head.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:58.330
Okay. I understand.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:00.370
Yes. Bye, now.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:02.910
How's Lizzy?

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.410
She's asleep.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.910
Don't worry. She has her friends with her.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.160
You should go to bed, too.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:17.290
No matter how long you wait for him,
that boy's not coming down.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.790
He may just disappear soon.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.040
What?

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.250
It's been a while
since he wandered his way here.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:29.200
<i>How old was he then?</i>

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.410
<i>He was already a formidable Exterminator.</i>

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.080
Curious?

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:38.040
It's a story from long ago

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:41.750
about a town on the edge of the Far East.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:07.790
-All right! Here we go!
-Darn!

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.750
Great work, bait.

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:22.830
Glad you didn't get eaten.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:24.250
Get up, shorty.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:29.000
Kidow, let's go.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:37.370
I guess he only listens to Lazarus.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.200
Out of the way!

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:41.410
Here it comes!

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:53.450
Fire!

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:07.580
A bug's desert.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:12.200
Lazarus, how long are we letting this kid
tag along?

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:16.700
If he can't keep up, he'll be left behind.
That's what I've told him.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.910
Then why pick him up in the first place?

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:29.040
Keep searching!

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:31.080
There should still be more!

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:35.790
No! No!

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:38.410
-Let go of me!
-Please! That's all we--

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:42.200
We risked our lives exterminating
those bugs! Be more grateful!

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:44.080
What a shame...

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:46.540
It's Looting Rights.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:51.950
That's how we Exterminators make a living.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:00.830
I heard you took in a kid.

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:03.700
You should really teach him some manners.

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:06.450
Put your gun down, he's okay.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:12.160
Nice to meet you, Kidow.
I'm Captain Edoardo Petrov

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.500
of the Allied Forces,
Far East Headquarters.

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:16.290
Why are you here?

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:20.870
Come on, can't a man just want to chat
with an old friend?

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:23.910
The Fort of Karakum?

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:28.250
He teaches the lost youth
how to exterminate

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:32.540
and brings them into his own organization.
The head of the Exterminators...

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:36.040
I'm surprised just how much someone
who served God can change.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.250
Leave if you have no business.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:42.040
You think anyone wants a military officer
wandering around their hideout?

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:44.660
I have a job.

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:46.950
The times we live in...

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:50.160
We humans have to stick together.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:54.700
We humans, huh?

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:24.750
What are you doing?

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.660
Just playing make-believe.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.830
Those who pray will find salvation.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:34.950
That's what we all believed.

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:38.290
But this is the outcome.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:58.200
It seems Lazarus taught Kidow
everything he needed to survive.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:03.250
<i>How to use weapons,</i>
<i>read and write, calculate...</i>

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.870
Your math's wrong, buddy!

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:06.950
Is that an accusation?

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:08.080
Let it go.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:10.040
The soldiers are looking at us.

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:14.040
You overcharged us, old man.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.120
Good job, Kidow!

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:18.950
As a reward,
we'll take you somewhere nice.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:25.450
Welcome.

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:29.950
So, what do you think
of the red light district, Kidow?

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:32.080
This also counts as social studies.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:35.370
So, you're the Kidow everyone talks about.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:45.290
Kara!

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:50.080
How can someone so small
be an Exterminator?

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:51.830
Oh, how cute.

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:57.000
But you're ten years too early
to come here, little guy.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:01.620
You're too early, she says, little Kidow.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.620
-My, you came?
-Oh, Kara!

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:14.120
What's the matter?

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:16.160
What's so great about women?

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.040
They're weak, but bossy.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.040
And they smell too sweet.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:25.580
Just let it go. Men aren't made to win
against women for some reason.

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:31.250
Lazarus! Why didn't you tell me
you were here?

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:34.450
-What the hell was that for?
-You still have this kid around?

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:35.700
I'm not afraid of you!

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:38.830
If you hurt me, the owner will kill you.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:40.040
You rang?

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:50.080
"Extermination terms"?

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:52.580
You know that it's been
established, right?

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:55.330
The border
between murder and extermination.

00:09:55.910 --> 00:10:00.450
Where to draw the line
within the 20 minutes

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:02.700
before the Cagaster outbreak is completed.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:07.540
The moment wings are identified,
human rights are discarded,

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:10.450
and murder turns into legal extermination.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:13.120
And the military
will oversee its enforcement.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:17.370
This isn't bad for you, either.

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:20.120
Instead of that barbaric Looting Right,

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:23.410
life will be more stable
with rewards from the military.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:25.580
Become the dogs of the military?

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:29.250
Just come to us when you want a treat.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.000
But if there are too many wild dogs,

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:35.080
we'll have to reconsider our options.

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:38.620
That's a warning from an old friend.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:42.450
The reason we live as wild dogs

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:45.160
is because we chose not to be sheep
scared of the bugs,

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:49.790
but beasts who will claw and cling to life
at any cost.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.870
If Cagasters aren't human,

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:57.080
then neither are the ones
who hunt them to live.

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:01.500
If you don't like that,
bring your sword instead of a warrant.

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:04.250
I'll take you on
as the head of the beasts.

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:11.080
-It's a Cagaster!
-Run!

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:14.660
Don't kill him!

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:18.830
-Mom!
-Take a good look!

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:21.790
Anyone who defends bugs
will be labeled a felon!

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:24.790
Dad!

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:30.040
Dad!

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:41.040
Kid, you're the child of a felon.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:43.000
You should live in shame.

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:44.790
Mom didn't do anything wrong.

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:49.750
What did you say? Are you guilty, too?

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:52.370
The one who took the bug's head
wasn't you.

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:55.790
You can act big once you do your job.

00:11:57.540 --> 00:11:58.450
Move out!

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:04.160
Murderer.

00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:15.660
Come on! Hurry!

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.040
-Go, go!
-Let's go!

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:20.700
-We'll drive the bugs there.
-Okay.

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:23.830
If we take too long, the military
will fry us along with the bugs!

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:25.040
Roger!

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:27.500
But can we really trust the military?

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:29.410
It's a huge job.

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:31.500
We know the risks.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.450
We've got a good group of them, boss!

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:48.500
-Okay, everyone fall back!
-Yes, sir!

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:50.620
Do it.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:58.830
Kidow!

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:06.910
You awake?

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:11.950
Where's Lazarus?

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:15.950
He's fine.
Even though everything turned out bad...

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:23.910
Lazarus,

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:26.950
why did you accept Petrov's job?

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:30.250
You knew the military wanted
to eliminate the Exterminators.

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:32.790
Without the military's jobs,

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.660
there's no way to maintain
this large organization, old man.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:38.870
So, it wasn't on purpose?

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:43.370
I know about your past.

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:46.080
Can you say that there was
no vengeance in your heart?

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:52.290
Lazarus!

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:57.120
Why did you save me?

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:03.200
I only told him to be grateful,
because you broke your arm saving him.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:04.700
What do you take me for?

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:06.370
If you ordered me to,

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:09.040
I would head fearlessly into any trap
or insect cage.

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:10.620
I'm not afraid to die!

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.410
It's better than a meaningless...

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:17.000
Do that again and I'll choose death!

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:24.620
<i>It's always the weak who suffer.</i>

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:28.370
Do you remember this child?

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:32.870
Karakum is too harsh for a child
to survive alone.

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:41.040
I once served God

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:43.870
and lived on prayers. However...

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:47.410
<i>for those who became rebels</i>
<i>in the world of bugs...</i>

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.000
<i>the voice of God was meaningless.</i>

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:55.660
Standing before my family's
horrifying corpses,

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.750
I despised and cursed all.

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:05.200
The bugs, the pillagers, my own impotence,
and even God.

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:09.250
I continued to kill bugs aimlessly.

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:11.290
That's all I could do.

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:17.000
Eventually, I was surrounded by people
who had nowhere else to go.

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:21.450
Before I knew it, I was the leader
of the rebels who I once despised.

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:24.620
Do you hate me, too?

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:30.750
I taught you that Exterminators
must stay a heartless sword.

00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:33.410
To prey on the weak without hesitation.

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:37.080
But I couldn't live like that.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:40.370
I pushed upon you the nonsense of one

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:43.910
who could neither become a sheep
nor a beast.

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:48.700
No! You're the Fort of Karakum!
You don't need to hesitate!

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:51.790
Just crush the military
and become king of Karakum!

00:15:55.750 --> 00:15:57.620
I plan to offer my head

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:01.250
to end this war between the military
and the Exterminators.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:02.250
What?

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:05.290
You should find and explore your own life.

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:10.330
My own life? What the hell is that?

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:13.500
I don't want that now.

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:17.870
I wanted to die believing in
and following you!

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:20.950
If you could just lead us,

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:24.790
I could continue to be a strong sword
that wouldn't even question death.

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:27.330
I don't have the power to do that.

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:31.950
I don't want to hear this!
Don't betray me!

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:33.080
Kidow...

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:45.250
Lazarus.

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:48.080
Now this can...

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:49.500
come to an end.

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:04.620
Lazarus...

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:07.870
Kidow.

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:10.580
Remember what I taught you?

00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:14.870
Always aim for the neck
when finishing a bug.

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:17.540
Lazarus.

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:37.410
I'm sorry.
Could you tell them I have a cold?

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:42.620
How long are you going to mope?

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:47.040
You can use my bath.
Get in there and clean yourself up.

00:17:58.080 --> 00:17:59.000
Kidow!

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:01.040
I killed him.

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:04.540
Lazarus taught me everything.

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:06.370
Gave me a home.

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:10.250
-Kidow.
-Lazarus is gone. Now there's...

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:12.700
no reason for me to be alive.

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:17.200
Why am I the one still alive?

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:39.000
Neither you nor Lazarus
did anything wrong.

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:43.290
This is just the world we live in now.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:46.410
You don't have to blame anyone.

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:08.040
I'm not old enough to be your mother,

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:09.910
but I can be your older sister.

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:13.580
No matter what happens
or who you make enemies with,

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:15.410
I'll be on your side.

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:19.000
<i>Okay.</i>

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:25.330
That kid stabbed Lazarus in the gut!

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:28.500
So, he did it before he turned into a bug?

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:31.160
-He won't get away with it!
-Don't.

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:35.620
The kid is the only one who can surpass
and claim Lazarus' throne.

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:38.750
He's the one who killed him, after all.

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:39.700
What!

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:42.660
We have our replacement for Lazarus.

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:45.950
We can't give the military an opening
to get at us.

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:48.290
You want to make that kid our boss?

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:51.830
Without a boss,
we're as good as dust in the wind.

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:54.410
Don't worry, it's just temporary.

00:19:55.370 --> 00:19:59.120
Eventually, we can make whoever
avenges Lazarus our next boss.

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:04.120
I was told Kidow is staying here.

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:09.290
Sorry, we don't serve young boys.

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:12.000
You would aid and abet a criminal?

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:15.660
Lazarus did show signs
of a Cagaster outbreak,

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:18.410
but we could not confirm wings.

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:22.370
In other words, in the eyes of the law,
Kidow committed a murder,

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:25.160
not an extermination.

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:28.620
Though,
I suppose we could cover that up for him.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:31.700
So, you plan to exploit him
for the rest of his life?

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:35.910
Many of our soldiers are fans of yours.

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:38.790
I don't want to have to use force, but...

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:40.370
Kidow!

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:45.620
Your reward for the extermination.

00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:58.750
Would you consider working for me?

00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:00.620
Even though I'm a murderer?

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:08.500
Lazarus and I grew up in a poor village.

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:12.500
Lazarus, who became the village pastor,
always invited me to his house

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.040
every time I would visit home.

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:18.200
He was happily surrounded
by family and friends.

00:21:18.950 --> 00:21:19.790
However...

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:23.330
<i>the village was consumed</i>
<i>by the bugs and rebels.</i>

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:26.290
<i>We each believed in different things,</i>

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:29.370
<i>but we shared an inability to do anything.</i>

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:33.790
Lazarus' child's name was Kidow.

00:21:35.700 --> 00:21:38.000
You were his replacement for his dead son.

00:21:38.700 --> 00:21:41.910
I don't want my friend
to lose another son.

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:44.200
Just sleep on it tonight.

00:22:02.450 --> 00:22:03.410
He got away?

00:22:04.200 --> 00:22:06.660
Apologies, sir. We're tracking him now.

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:07.830
That's not necessary.

00:22:08.580 --> 00:22:10.080
<i>He's a smart child.</i>

00:22:10.870 --> 00:22:13.410
<i>He knows what he needs to do.</i>

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:31.410
<i>I wanted to make Lazarus</i>
<i>into a crucified god.</i>

00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:35.200
<i>I wanted a god to turn to.</i>

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:38.330
<i>If I gave everything to God,</i>

00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:40.950
<i>there would be nothing to fear.</i>

00:22:42.200 --> 00:22:45.580
<i>If Lazarus didn't hesitate,</i>
<i>I wouldn't, either.</i>

00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:48.500
<i>I killed my father...</i>

00:22:49.750 --> 00:22:51.120
<i>and gained a god.</i>

00:22:52.540 --> 00:22:53.910
<i>I won't hesitate anymore.</i>

00:22:55.330 --> 00:22:57.000
<i>The god who bathed my heart in blood</i>

00:22:57.750 --> 00:23:01.200
<i>and was crucified for me will</i>
<i>forevermore...</i>

00:23:02.160 --> 00:23:03.950
<i>will forevermore be at my side.</i>

00:23:05.450 --> 00:23:08.620
<i>Kara, I wanted to ask my sister a favor.</i>

00:23:10.290 --> 00:23:12.330
<i>Please hold on to the god...</i>

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:16.580
<i>Lazarus couldn't abandon,</i>
<i>along with my real name.</i>

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.580
<i>There's no other place for my soul</i>
<i>to return to if I die.</i>

00:23:23.330 --> 00:23:24.250
<i>Kara.</i>

00:23:25.160 --> 00:23:26.500
<i>This is the world we live in,</i>

00:23:27.500 --> 00:23:28.750
<i>but please find happiness.</i>

00:23:29.950 --> 00:23:31.410
What happiness?

00:23:33.790 --> 00:23:36.370
I don't want it. Not one like this.

00:23:41.700 --> 00:23:43.200
Do you feel sorry for him?

00:23:45.250 --> 00:23:46.290
I don't know.

00:23:47.080 --> 00:23:51.160
Yes, I suppose a scar becomes a part
of who you are.

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:53.790
It's not something you try to heal.

00:23:55.120 --> 00:23:56.540
There are some people

00:23:57.500 --> 00:23:59.330
who can't breathe without the pain.

00:24:11.080 --> 00:24:12.000
You need something?

00:24:13.040 --> 00:24:15.290
I was wondering if you were hungry.

00:24:16.450 --> 00:24:18.950
I'm glad to see you're more energetic
than I thought.

00:24:19.540 --> 00:24:21.040
I'll bring tea.

00:24:23.790 --> 00:24:25.750
You came to pity me, right?

00:24:27.040 --> 00:24:29.790
I just killed someone I knew.

00:24:30.830 --> 00:24:32.790
I'm so worked up that I can't sleep.

00:24:34.790 --> 00:24:37.040
I won't take long if you stay still.

00:24:38.540 --> 00:24:40.200
No, don't.

00:24:41.120 --> 00:24:42.040
No!

00:24:42.410 --> 00:24:43.870
No! Stop!

00:24:44.660 --> 00:24:46.700
Help! Dad!

00:24:50.540 --> 00:24:53.000
Seriously? Okay, I'm out.

00:24:54.120 --> 00:24:57.830
Guess I'll need to pay someone
who's actually sexy.

00:24:58.790 --> 00:24:59.870
I don't pity you!

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:03.250
What's that for?

00:25:03.370 --> 00:25:06.290
Why would I pity you? I wouldn't do that.

00:25:06.830 --> 00:25:09.000
You knew I wasn't sexy.

00:25:09.250 --> 00:25:12.410
So, don't do that from the start.
From the start...

00:25:13.500 --> 00:25:16.040
You should've just ignored it all
from the start.

00:25:16.500 --> 00:25:17.950
Both me and Mr. Qasim.

00:25:18.660 --> 00:25:20.750
If you're going to get this upset
and perverse,

00:25:20.830 --> 00:25:22.500
maybe you should quit exterminating!

00:25:24.250 --> 00:25:25.160
If you had,

00:25:25.580 --> 00:25:28.330
I wouldn't have fallen in love
with someone like you.

00:25:31.080 --> 00:25:33.120
I wouldn't have had to cry so much.

00:25:35.160 --> 00:25:36.200
So, why?

00:25:37.580 --> 00:25:39.620
Why can't I hate you?

00:25:42.660 --> 00:25:45.290
I can't quit being an Exterminator.

00:25:47.160 --> 00:25:49.540
I'm prepared to cut off the head of anyone

00:25:50.120 --> 00:25:51.910
who becomes a bug in front of me.

00:25:52.700 --> 00:25:53.620
But...

00:25:54.580 --> 00:25:57.160
I'm also not ready
to live my life with someone.

00:25:59.700 --> 00:26:00.620
Sorry.

00:26:01.120 --> 00:26:02.040
For everything.

00:26:11.540 --> 00:26:13.700
Fine, do whatever you want.

00:26:14.660 --> 00:26:16.200
What a waste.

00:26:16.910 --> 00:26:18.700
I'll eat it, just leave them.

00:26:18.790 --> 00:26:21.290
-What? But...
-Please.

00:26:23.250 --> 00:26:25.540
Don't complain if you get sick.

00:26:31.700 --> 00:26:33.700
Apparently, men are no match for women.

00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:36.830
That's what Qasim and my old man said.

00:26:37.330 --> 00:26:39.330
What? That's a weird thing to say.

00:26:40.500 --> 00:26:41.500
Yeah.

00:26:42.120 --> 00:26:43.040
You're right.

00:28:37.540 --> 00:28:40.040
Subtitle translation by Zensho Yamamoto
